WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.850
Here is a cubic equation: z cubed plus
p z squared plus q z plus r equals zero.

2
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.870
You can't see the coefficients.

3
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.960
All you know is that
every one of them is real.

4
00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.670
One root is revealed: two plus i.

5
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.340
A cubic has three roots.

6
00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.760
Does knowing just this one, and
that the coefficients are real,

7
00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:23.580
force any other root?

8
00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:25.380
If so, which?

9
00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:29.540
In this mission, you'll solve polynomial
equations with real coefficients from

10
00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.420
a given complex root.

11
00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.250
You'll prove De Moivre's
theorem by induction.

12
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.410
And you'll use it to build
multiple-angle identities,

13
00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.470
such as cos three theta.

14
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.480
Your mission: find the other root that
is guaranteed when a real cubic has root

15
00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:45.710
two plus i.
